      "explanation": "(A) In the first compound, because of +I effect of CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>- group electron density increses on N atom.\n<br><br>(B) In the second compound, because of +I effect of two CH<sub>3</sub>CH<sub>2</sub>- group electron density is more on N atom than first compound so it is more basic than compound A.\n<br><br>(C) Three -CH<sub>3</sub> group creates steric hindrance around N atom, for that reason N atom can't donate lone pair easily.\n<br><br>(D) Here lone pair of N atom, perticipate in resonance with benzene ring so N atom can't donate lone pair. That is why it is least basic among this four compounds.\n<br><br>So correct order is D &lt; C &lt; A &lt; B."
